-- title:
--   Level-ℓ fine family on connected Noetherian bases
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$ (`hrr`), and a nonzero natural number $N$ with $r \nmid N$ (`hrN`), $\bar r \nmid N$ (`hrbarN`) and $N$ squarefree (`hN`). A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`), $\mathcal O$ being $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), with $\#(\mathcal O/\pi) = r$ (`hres`) and $(r) = (\pi)$ (`hunr`); a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. A characteristic-zero domain $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal being maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element satisfying a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^r \bmod \pi$ (`hFr`). A homomorphism $v_{\det} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ with `hvdet`: $v_{\det}(g) = n$ exactly when $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some $u \in \mathcal O^\times$.
--
--   **Quaternionic moduli.** Rationals $a, b$ with `hB`: $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is a division algebra at a finite place exactly when the place lies over $r$ or $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`). A scheme $\mathcal X$ with $f : \mathcal X \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathcal O$ and point maps $\mathrm{pt}$, satisfying `h𝒳` = `IsCoarseModuli`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with pullback, bijectivity on points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property, for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure. An integer $n \ge 3$ (`hn`) with $r \nmid n$, $\bar r \nmid n$ (`hrn`, `hrbarn`) and $\gcd(n,N)=1$ (`hnN`); $M$, $f_M$, $\mathrm{ptF}$ with `hM` = `IsFineModuli`: the points of $M$ classify pairs (fake elliptic curve, full level-$n$ structure) up to isomorphism, compatibly with pullback. A group $G$, $\rho : G \to \operatorname{Aut} M$ and $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ with `hρ` = `IsLevelTwistAction` (each $\rho(h)$ lies over the base; twisting a full level structure by $\chi(h)$ moves the point by $\rho(h)$; $\chi$ is multiplicative, injective and surjective modulo $n$). A forgetful map $p : M \to \mathcal X$ with `hp` ($p$ followed by $f$ is $f_M$), `hρp` ($G$-invariance) and `hp_pt` (compatibility on points).
--
--   **Tower and Atkin–Lehner data.** For every prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$, schemes $\mathcal Y_\ell$ with $g_\ell$ and point maps $\mathrm{ptT}_\ell$ satisfying `h𝒴` = `IsCoarseModuliT` for pairs (curve, extra level-$\ell$ structure); degeneracy maps $d_0, d_1$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) realising on points the forgetting of the extra level (`hd₀`) and the passage to a level-$\ell$ isogenous curve (`hd₁`). Maps $a_r, a_{\bar r} : \mathcal X \to \mathcal X$ over $f$ (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion side.** Rationals $a_1, b_1$ with `hdef`: $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$ and ramification exactly at $\bar r$. A maximal order $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`), an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ (`hR₁`) with $R_1 \le \Lambda_1$ (`hRΛ₁`); an adelic unit $n_1 \in \mathrm{primeHeckeSet}\,R_1\,r$ (`hn₁`) with $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1$ Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_0 : \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); the height-one prime $v$ containing $r$ (`hv`). A subgroup $\Gamma^t$ equal to $\mathrm{awayUnits}\,R_1\,v$ (`hΓt`), i.e. the units lying in the local unit groups of $R_1$ at all places other than $v$. Elements $s_\ell$ and adelic units $sf_\ell$ with `hs` (four clauses per $\ell$: $sf_\ell$ is the diagonal image of $s_\ell$ away from $r$, is $1$ at $r$, the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}$ or $\mathrm{primeHeckeSet}$ of $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1$ according as $\ell \mid N$ or not, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$); subgroups $\Gamma^t_\ell = \Gamma^t \cap s_\ell \Gamma^t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $\bar w$ with `hwbar`: $\mathrm{nrd}(\bar w) = \bar r$ and conjugation by $\bar w$ preserves $\Gamma^t$.
--
--   **Reduction data and the action on $A_0$.** `hΛℤ`: $\mathbb Z \subseteq \Lambda$; a map $\mathrm{coord} : \Lambda \to W(\mathbb F_{r^2})^2$ with `hcoord` = `IsOrderCoord` (additive, injective, normalised at $1$, twisted-multiplicative, with dense image and the prescribed trace identity). A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ in two variables, with `hA₀`: $A_0$ is a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$. Endomorphisms $e, e' : \Gamma^t \to \operatorname{End}(A_0.A)$ over the base (`he`) with degrees $\deg$, subject to the group `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` (summarised here): each $e_\gamma$ is part of an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg \gamma}$ preserving the level-$N$ structure; $e$ is multiplicative and sends rational scalars to multiplications, both up to $r$-power multiplications, and conversely only scalars act as multiplications; after conjugation by a single $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ the induced action on the formal group matches $\iota_0(\gamma)$ up to a power of $r$ under any injective $E_0$ on the centraliser of $X_0$'s action and $\varpi$; $e$ labels the chosen full level-$n$ structure by elements of $\Lambda$ multiplicatively modulo $n$; and every level-preserving $r$-power isogeny on a geometric specialisation of $A_0$ comes from some $\gamma \in \Gamma^t$. A further order $R_2 \le R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) with $r$-power denominators for $R_1$ (`hR₂r`) and $\hat e : R_2 \to \operatorname{End}(A_0.A)$ over the base (`hê`), subject to `hE5a`, `hE5b1`, `hE5b2`, `hE5b3`, `hE5c`, `hE5d`, `hE5e`, `hE5g` (summarised here: $\hat e$ is additive on points, commutes with the $\Lambda$-action, preserves the level, is multiplicative with $\hat e(1) = \mathrm{id}$ and $\hat e(m) = [m]$, satisfies $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x) = [\mathrm{nrd}\,x]$, agrees with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma^t$, and is compared to $\iota_0$ on the formal group by a common conjugator; $R_2$ is stable under the main involution). A twin maximal order $\Lambda_1^s$ with $\Lambda_1 \cap \Lambda_1^s = R_1$ (`hΛ₁s`, `hR₁Λ₁s`, `htwin`), an order $R_2' \le \Lambda_1^s$ with $r$-power denominators for $\Lambda_1^s$ and $R_2 \le R_2'$ (`hR₂'`, `hR₂'o`, `hR₂'r`, `hR₂R₂'`), and $\hat e'$ over the base (`hê'`), subject to `hE6a`, `hE6b1`, `hE6b2`, `hE6b3`, `hE6c`, `hE6d`, `hE6e1`, `hE6e2`, `hE6f` (summarised here: the same additivity, $\Lambda$-equivariance, multiplicativity, norm and involution properties, $\hat e'$ extends $\hat e$, $\hat e'$ is injective, and an element killing the $q$-torsion for a prime $q \neq r$ is divisible by $q$ after multiplication by a power of $r$).
--
--   **Drinfeld side.** A ring map $\iota : W(\mathbb F_{r^2}) \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/r$ of height $4$ (`hΦ`, `hΦ4`), a moduli package $MD$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), a family $\eta$ of maps from rigidified modules to $MD$ with `hη` (three clauses: $\eta$ separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, is compatible with base change, and is locally surjective on a Zariski cover), and an injective $E_0$ on the centraliser of $\Phi$'s action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ with `hE₀` (its image is the integral matrices up to a fixed power of $r$). A comparison $eD$ between $\mathrm{G}(MD)$ and $(O^{\mathrm{nr}}\text{-points}) \times \Omega$, with `hnatD` (naturality), `hbijD` (bijectivity), `hfstD` (it computes the structure map), `hGLD` ($\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-equivariance for the twisted action), `hPiD` and `hPiexD` ($\pi$-translations correspond to one Frobenius twist, and exist). A map $\kappa$ with `hκ` relating the two residue quotients, and $n_0$, $\beta_0$ with `hβ₀`: $\beta_0$ is an isogeny from $\Phi$ to $X_0$ reduced along $\kappa$, of height $4n_0$. A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner datum on $A_0$.** A curve $A_0^w$ with maps $a_w, a_w', b_w, b_w'$ and the requisite factorisations (`haw`, `haw'`, `hbw`, `habw`), `hALw` (an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$), `hBSw` (an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ back to $A_0$), `hBSwlev` (level preservation), and `hJOINTw` (a single conjugator simultaneously matching the action of all $e_\gamma$ with $\iota_0(\gamma)$ and that of $a_w$ followed by $b_w$ with $\iota_0(\bar w)$, up to powers of $r$, on the formal group).
--
--   **The map $\Xi$ and its equivariance.** A map $\Xi$ sending a rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra to a point of $\mathrm{G}(MD)$, with `hΞleg` (over a base with only trivial idempotents the structure map of the image is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (compatibility with pullbacks of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves matching the rigidifications up to $r$-power multiplications) and `hΞdef` (the image is computed by $\eta$ applied to a rigidified formal module transported from $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$ with twist index $j \le 1$). An element $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with `heqΓ`, `heqW`, `heqS`: translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$, by the $\bar r$-Atkin–Lehner datum, and by a level-$\ell$ isogeny datum attached to $s$, moves $\Xi$ by the action of $r^c \cdot g_0 \iota_0(\gamma) g_0^{-1}$, $r^c \cdot g_0 \iota_0(\bar w) g_0^{-1}$ and $r^c \cdot g_0 \iota_0(\ell s^{-1}) g_0^{-1}$ respectively.
--
--   **The family on $M$.** A homomorphism $\theta^t : \Gamma^t \to G$ and a family $\Theta_f$ sending a triple (an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$, a Deligne datum over $B$, an element of $G$) over a $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ to a $B$-point of $M$ over $\mathcal O$, with `hnat` (naturality), `hG` ($G$-equivariance through $\rho$), `hi'` (invariance under the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma^t$ combined with $\theta^t(\gamma)$), `het` (unique infinitesimal lifting along surjections with square-zero-like kernels) and `hfib` (two triples over an algebraically closed field have the same image exactly when they differ by some $\gamma \in \Gamma^t$ in the prescribed way). Further clauses `hC0e`, `hC0u` (existence and uniqueness of the normalised level transport of $P_0$ along a rigidification), `hC1e`, `hC1u`, `hC1p` (existence, uniqueness up to an isomorphism of rigidified curves, and pullback of an "even" rigidified curve with prescribed image $(\psi, P)$ under $eD \circ \Xi$ twisted by $g_0^{-1}$), `hC2`, `hC2c` (the value of $\Theta_f$ at $(\psi,P,1)$ is the point of $M$ of $(E, P_n)$, and its composite with $p$ is the point of $\mathcal X$ of $E$), and `hC3`, `hC4`, `hC4pi`, `hC5` (the equivariance of this correspondence under the twisted action of $\Gamma^t$, of general $\iota_0(h)$ up to $r$-powers, of $\pi$-translations, and the description of isomorphisms between two even curves with the same $\psi$ over an algebraically closed field).
--
--   **Extra-level data.** Extra level-$\ell$ structures $C_0(\ell)$ on $A_0$ for all tower primes $\ell$, together with curves $A_0^s(\ell)$ and maps $a_s, a_s', b_s, b_s'$ with the factorisations (`has`, `has'`, `hbs`, `habs`), `hLIs` (level-$\ell$ isogeny quotient by $C_0(\ell)$), `hBSs` (isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_s(\ell)}$), `hBSslev` (level preservation) and `hJOINTs` (joint formal comparison with $\iota_0(\overline{s_\ell})$); `hSTAB`: $e_\gamma$ preserves the subgroup $C_0(\ell)$ exactly when $\gamma \in \Gamma^t_\ell$. Clauses `hCLe`, `hCLu`: for $\ell \neq r$ invertible on $B$, an extra level-$\ell$ structure on $E$ transporting a given one on $A_0$ along a rigidification exists, and any two such have the same points. Families $\Theta_T(\ell)$ of $B$-points of $\mathcal Y_\ell$ with `hnatT` (naturality) and `hVT` (the value of $\Theta_T(\ell)$ at $(\psi,P)$ is the point of $\mathcal Y_\ell$ of $(E, C)$ whenever $(E,\varrho)$ is even with image $(\psi,P)$ and $C$ transports $C_0(\ell)$).
--
--   **The fixed tower prime.** A prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$, a scheme $M_\ell$ with $f_{M_\ell}$ and point maps $\mathrm{ptF}_\ell$ satisfying `hMℓ` = `IsFineModuliT` for triples (curve, full level $n$, extra level $\ell$); $\pi_\ell : M_\ell \to M$ over the base (`hπℓf`) forgetting the extra level on points (`hπℓ`); $p_\ell : M_\ell \to \mathcal Y_\ell$ over the base (`hpℓg`) compatible on points (`hpℓ`); an action $\rho_\ell : G \to \operatorname{Aut} M_\ell$ over the base (`hρℓf`) lifting $\rho$ along $\pi_\ell$ (`hρℓπ`), fixing $p_\ell$ (`hρℓp`), and acting by level twists: if an isomorphism exhibits $u'$ as the $\chi(h)$-twist of $u$ and matches the extra level structures $C$, $C'$, then the point of $(u', C')$ is the point of $(u,C)$ followed by $\rho_\ell(h)$ (`hρℓtw`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a family $\Theta^c$ which assigns, to every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ such that the image of $\pi$ in $B$ is nilpotent and every idempotent of $B$ is $0$ or $1$, a map from pairs $(\psi, P)$ consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and a Deligne datum $P$ over $B$, to the set of morphisms $\operatorname{Spec} B \to M_\ell$ whose composite with $f_{M_\ell}$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathcal O \to B$, such that the following two statements hold.
--
--   First, naturality: for all Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$, $B'$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent and whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi : B \to B'$ and every pair $x$ over $B$, the value of $\Theta^c$ over $B'$ at the image of $x$ (that is, at $\varphi \circ \psi$ together with the base change of the Deligne datum) equals $\operatorname{Spec} \varphi$ followed by $\Theta^c(x)$.
--
--   Second, the value: for every such $B$, every $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$, every Deligne datum $P$ over $B$, every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, every rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ relative to $A_0$ along $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-v_{\det}(g_0)}$, every full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on $E$ and every extra level-$\ell$ structure $C$ on $E$, if
--
--   (i) the structure map of $\Xi(\langle E, \varrho\rangle)$ is $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-v_{\det}(g_0)}$ (the pair is even),
--
--   (ii) the twisted action of $g_0^{-1}$ carries $eD(\Xi(\langle E,\varrho\rangle))$ to $(\psi, P)$, that is, the first component of the target is the $(-v_{\det}(g_0^{-1}))$-Frobenius twist of the source's and the second is the pullback of the source's Deligne datum along $g_0$,
--
--   (iii) $P_n$ is a normalised level transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho$ for the data $\mathrm{Fr}$, $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$, $\Phi$, $\iota$, $\mathrm{coord}$, and
--
--   (iv) $C$ transports $C_0(\ell)$: for every scheme $T$, every morphism $t'$ from $T$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $B/\pi$ and every point $R$ of $\varrho.E_b$ over $t'$, if $R$ followed by $\varrho.g_b$ factors through $C.\mathrm{levK}$ then $R$ followed by $\varrho.\varphi$ and then $\varrho.g_A$ factors through the level map of $C_0(\ell)$,
--
--   then the morphism underlying $\Theta^c_B(\psi, P)$ equals the morphism underlying $\mathrm{ptF}_\ell$ evaluated over $B$, at the structure map $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathcal O \to B$, on the pair $\langle E, P_n\rangle$ together with $C$.
--
--   This is the construction step of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation at the level-$\ell$ stage of the Hecke tower: over connected Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent bases, the formal points of the $\pi$-adic upper half-plane (twisted by the unramified base $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$) are turned into points of the fine moduli scheme $M_\ell$ of curves with full level $n$ and an extra level-$\ell$ subgroup, with the value prescribed on even rigidified curves. It is used by the companion statement which upgrades this family to one compatible with the projection $\pi_\ell$, the Hecke map $p_\ell$ and the twist action $\rho_\ell$.
